<% content_for :title, "About" %>
<% content_for :description, "Grouparty is a free collection of party games you play together: one shared screen, and everyone joins from their own phone. Built for fun by Daniel Arenas." %>

<div class="min-h-screen py-12 px-4 sm:px-6">
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto text-slate-300 leading-relaxed space-y-6">
    <%= render "pages/header", title: "About #{SeoHelper::SITE_NAME}", subtitle: "Party games for one big screen and everyone's phones." %>

    <section class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">What is <%= SeoHelper::SITE_NAME %>?</h2>
      <p>
        <%= SeoHelper::SITE_NAME %> is a free collection of multiplayer party games made for groups in the same room.
        One person opens a game on a TV, laptop or tablet: that is the host screen everybody watches.
        Everyone else scans the QR code with their phone, types a nickname and plays from their own device.
      </p>
      <p>
        There is nothing to install and no account to create. It works in any modern web browser, so a family
        dinner, a classroom break or a night with friends can turn into a game in less than a minute.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">The games</h2>
      <p>
        The collection mixes very different kinds of play: timed trivia, social deduction, memory challenges,
        color guessing, number hunting, word matching, tank battles and submarine combat. Every game is designed so
        the shared screen tells the story while each phone becomes a private controller, which means you can keep
        secrets, race against each other and see the results together.
      </p>
      <% if (games = Game.order(name: :asc).to_a).any? %>
        <ul class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3">
          <% games.each do |game| %>
            <li class="bg-slate-800 border border-slate-700 rounded-xl px-4 py-3">
              <p class="text-white font-bold"><%= game.name %></p>
              <p class="text-slate-400 text-sm"><%= game.description %></p>
            </li>
          <% end %>
        </ul>
      <% end %>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">Who makes it</h2>
      <p>
        Hi, I'm <strong class="text-white">Daniel Arenas</strong>, a software developer. I built
        <%= SeoHelper::SITE_NAME %> just for fun, because I wanted simple games to play with friends and family
        where nobody has to download an app. I keep adding new games and improving the existing ones.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can see more of my work on GitHub:
        <%= link_to "github.com/daniel-arenas-ror", PagesController::GITHUB_URL,
                    class: "text-purple-400 hover:text-purple-300 underline", target: "_blank", rel: "noopener" %>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">Free to play</h2>
      <p>
        <%= SeoHelper::SITE_NAME %> is free. To help pay for the servers, the site may show ads served by Google.
        You can read how that works in the <%= link_to "Privacy Policy", privacy_path, class: "text-purple-400 hover:text-purple-300 underline" %>.
        Ideas, bug reports or game suggestions are always welcome on the
        <%= link_to "Contact page", contact_path, class: "text-purple-400 hover:text-purple-300 underline" %>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>

  <%= ad_slot :page, css: "max-w-3xl mx-auto mt-12" %>
</div>
